<title>USA: Keycorp to sell Wyoming unit for $135 mln.</title>
<headline>Keycorp to sell Wyoming unit for $135 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>KeyCorp said on Tuesday it reached a definitive agreement to sell KeyBank National Association of Wyoming to Community First Bankshares Inc for $135 million in cash.</p>
<p>KeyBank has 28 branches with total deposits of $1 billion and loans of $850 million, of which Key will retain $350 million.</p>
<p>Community First Bankshares is based in Fargo, N.D.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
